{"name":"Old Ivory","hex":"#ffffcb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"},{"term":"ivory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The hard white form of dentin which forms the tusks of elephants, walruses and other animals.","A creamy white color, the color of ivory."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of ivory.","Resembling or having the colour of ivory."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ivory","blocks":[{"text":"Ivory is a hard, white material from the tusks and teeth of animals, that consists mainly of dentin, one of the physical structures of teeth and tusks. The chemical structure of the teeth and tusks of mammals is the same, regardless of the species of origin, but ivory contains structures of mineralized collagen. The trade in certain tusks and teeth other than elephant is well established and widespread; therefore, \"ivory\" can correctly be used to describe any mammalian teeth or tusks of commercial interest which are large enough to be carved or scrimshawed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Horn_Louvre_OA4069.jpg/330px-Horn_Louvre_OA4069.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivory","wikidata":"Q82001"},{"title":"Ivory (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Ivory is an off-white color named after, and derived from, the material made from the tusks and teeth of certain animals, such as the elephant and the walrus. It has a very slight tint of yellow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Decorated_ivory.JPG/330px-